**How to implement.** Applying a split attaches the file once and maps each group to its experiment by the key's rows, creating the ticked offers' setups and experiments (001 §P `MatchByTemplate`; 001 §K 'match each group by the naming template, list the unmatched groups and offer to create setups for them'; 001 §E 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into `data/`'; the S9.2 mapper's request: a split group is a `KeyedDataRows` of one `MappedAttachment`; the precedent of `GenerateSetupGrid`, step 276: setups and experiments written in order, the first failure stopping the run). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`, each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3: (1) `MatchByTemplate` (apply the split: attach the file once, map each matched group, create each ticked offer), documented in one line and refused by the read-only guard of step 185. With no split (`dataSplitOpt = None`) it changes nothing. With `dataSplitOpt = Some s`, `s.creating` not empty and a draft that cannot record an experiment (no chosen axis or no capture the detectors allow, as `RecordExperiment` requires, step 278), it sets `kitStatus` to `Not split — a new experiment records the Experiments draft's scan: choose a variable there, or tick no offer.` and writes nothing. (2) Otherwise `model.experimentData.attachDataFile s.file` (step 305) attaches the file once, copied into `data/` from outside the kit or recorded in place (steps 133, 134); an error sets `kitStatus` `Not attached — <e.describe>` and writes nothing else. With the attachment, each group of `s.split.groups` in order: an `ExperimentForGroup name` group's experiment (the collection's of that name) takes `attachDataFile` of `{ attachment; profile = s.profile; rows = KeyedDataRows key; exclusions = [] }` (steps 291, 313) and is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment`; a `SetupOfferForGroup offer` group whose key `s.creating` holds records `offer.setup` through `recordSetup` (step 260) when `kitSetups` lacks it (by equality), then appends a new experiment of the draft's scan over `offer.setup.reference` named `offer.experiment`, as `RecordExperiment` appends one (step 278, never editing the draft's own), which takes the same keyed attachment before it is recorded, so each experiment file is written once; an unticked offer and a `GroupWithoutMatch` group write nothing. The first write that fails stops the run: the collection and `kitSetups` hold what was written, and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. (3) On success `dataSplitOpt` is `None`, `kitSetups` holds the new setups in name order, each experiment given data has its badge computed by the one private validation function (steps 136, 295), and `kitStatus` is `Attached <the file's leaf> to <a> experiment(s): <m> matched, <c> created with <s> new setup(s); <u> group(s) left unattached.`, `u` counting the unticked offers and the unmatched groups. The table, `activeSetupOpt`, the draft and `reviewedDataOpt` are unchanged. No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `DataSplitModelTests` (step 319), over its fixture after `SplitByColumn (<the file>, ImportProfileName.phoneRoiCsv)`: `applying a split attaches the file once and gives each matched experiment the rows of its key, and an unticked offer creates nothing`: `MatchByTemplate` leaves `data/<the file's leaf>` holding the file's exact bytes once, `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd`'s data that attachment mapped by `Phone ROI CSV` to `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey "LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd")` with no exclusion, its file read back through `readExperiments` holding the same, `model.dataBadgeOf` of it `ValidatedDataBadge` of 2 points, no setup or experiment file added, `dataSplitOpt` `None` and `kitStatus` `Attached <leaf> to 1 experiment(s): 1 matched, 0 created with 0 new setup(s); 3 group(s) left unattached.`. `a ticked offer records its setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its rows`: with both offers ticked (`ToggleSplitOffer`), `MatchByTemplate` writes `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd.setup-json` and no second `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd.setup-json`, the experiments `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd-2` over `LP1-(QZ#45)-LPd` revision 1 and `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` over `LP1-(QZ2#0)-LPd` revision 1, each of the draft's scan and mapped to the rows of its key, and `kitStatus` naming 3 experiments, 2 created and 1 new setup; E1's draft still edits what it edited. `a split with a ticked offer and no draft scan, or with no split, writes nothing`: after `ExpNew` (no axis) with an offer ticked, `MatchByTemplate` sets the `Not split —` status and every file's bytes are unchanged, and `MatchByTemplate` after `CancelDataSplit` changes nothing. `KitWindowModelTests`: `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `MatchByTemplate`, with its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After `MatchByTemplate` lands, applying a split MUST attach the file once and give each matched experiment the keyed rows of its group through the chosen profile, record each ticked offer's setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its keyed rows, leave unticked and unmatched groups unattached, and write nothing for a ticked offer without a draft scan or a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `applying a split attaches the file once and gives each matched experiment the rows of its key, and an unticked offer creates nothing`, `a ticked offer records its setup when the kit lacks it and a new experiment of the draft's scan with its rows` and `a split with a ticked offer and no draft scan, or with no split, writes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
